# This directory is intentionally tracked (empty) so it exists as a mount
# point in the OCI content image (deploy/content.Dockerfile COPYs .agents/).
#
# The deploy nests a writable `plans` emptyDir at
# /opt/kube-platform-agent/.agents/plans, INSIDE the read-only image volume.
# A read-only image layer cannot have a directory created in it at mount
# time, so the mount point must already exist in the image — that's what
# this file guarantees. At runtime the emptyDir shadows this file.
#
# record_plan derives plansDir = agentsDir + "/plans" and writes plan
# artifacts here (see pkg/tools/record_plan.go). Locally the dir is created
# on demand; in the read-only image volume it must be pre-baked.
